data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":81,"item_id":"rs_037dac643fd387e8016ac9643684548196b76bda23548cc75c","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering migration tests**\n\nI'm thinking about managing my 8k token budget for updates. I should update the last summary and include an archived restart test before anything else is unchecked. For the migration test, it sounds like I could add a prior fixture using SQLite to test the old schema. I'm wondering if a separate test is really necessary, or if I should just add an initial empty database before the test starts."}

